                <pb facs="0759" n="623" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg623"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.79611 Tri-Motors Safety Airways/97:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in
                        Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Schoenfeld</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-08-17T15:00:00-04:00">August 17, 1929—3
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>46. If the Brazilian Government inquires you may say for the information of the
                    Minister of Transportation that the Department is informed that the New York,
                    Rio and Buenos Aires Line, Incorporated, is American owned and financed solely
                    by American money and that Trimotors Safety Airways, Incorporated, is a
                    subsidiary of the New York, Rio and Buenos Aires Line entirely owned by it and
                    with no foreign interest or control.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Castle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
